 ## Background
-This configuration originates from the JAX-based implementation of Neural Graphics Primitives (NGP) or similar radiance field frameworks, as seen in the `jaxngp` repository [S1, unofficial]. It is designed to optimize the MLPs and appearance embeddings in neural radiance fields. The use of selective L2 decay is a known technique in NeRF training to prevent over-regularization of positional encodings, which are critical for high-frequency detail representation [S1, unofficial].
